WEBVTT

1
00:51:08.418 --> 00:51:17.418
Come to Jesus. Stay with Him inside. Come to Jesus. Thank Him that He has set you free from sins.

2
00:51:18.418 --> 00:51:25.418
Come to Jesus. Pray to Him if you are struggling to let go of certain things.

3
00:51:25.418 --> 00:51:30.418
Just say it to Him. Start talking to Him. Begin to say honest things to Him.

4
00:51:30.418 --> 00:51:41.418
Talk to Him like a best friend. He is your very best friend. He is with you.

5
00:51:41.418 --> 00:51:47.418
Just speak to Him. Lord, I am struggling with this. Lord, I want to lay it down at the cross.

6
00:51:47.418 --> 00:51:55.418
Lord, this goes wrong every time. Lord, help me with that. Be honest with Jesus. You must be honest with Him.

7
00:51:55.418 --> 00:52:04.418
You know, He already knows everything about your life, but He is waiting for you to be truly honest with Him and start talking to Him.

8
00:52:04.418 --> 00:52:13.418
Say Lord, thank you that this is going well in my life. Thank you Lord that my family is healthy. Thank you that I have a career. Thank you that I have work.

9
00:52:13.418 --> 00:52:17.418
But this is still not easy, Lord. Will You help me with that?

10
00:52:17.418 --> 00:52:23.418
Maybe there is pride in your life. Maybe there are sins in your life. Maybe there are things you just need to lay down at the cross.

11
00:52:23.418 --> 00:52:30.418
Maybe there is fear in your life. Lay down fear. Don't just listen to my words, but go into your prayer with Jesus yourself.

12
00:52:30.418 --> 00:52:38.418
We are here in a holy moment. We are here celebrating what Jesus has done for us. We can lay everything down at the cross. Everything.

13
00:52:38.418 --> 00:52:46.418
Fear, worries, sin, rudeness, unforgiveness.

14
00:52:46.418 --> 00:52:55.418
If there are things done against you that you find difficult to forgive others for. Forgive it, for Jesus has forgiven it at the cross.

15
00:52:55.418 --> 00:53:05.418
Come to Jesus. Maybe there are things that have happened that you think, I don't know how this will turn out well. Lay it down at the cross of Jesus.

16
00:53:05.418 --> 00:53:12.418
Lord, how should I approach this? How do I get out of this situation? Lay it down with Jesus. He knows how to do it.

17
00:53:13.418 --> 00:53:20.418
He is not only a savior, but He also resolves it for you. For He has the way out. He has all the wisdom.

18
00:53:22.418 --> 00:53:33.418
Parents, speak to Jesus for your children. Bless your children at this moment. I want to give attention to these prayers. Stay in prayer.

19
00:53:33.418 --> 00:53:37.418
Speak the names of your children. Bring them to Jesus.

20
00:53:38.418 --> 00:53:48.418
Name the names of your children. I bring my children to Jesus. Maybe they are not here at this moment. Maybe they are not walking with Jesus at this moment.

21
00:53:48.418 --> 00:53:58.418
Bring them to the cross. Name their name. Cover them under the blood of Jesus. The Bible says, parents in Christ, their children are sanctified.

22
00:53:58.418 --> 00:54:04.418
Perhaps they have not yet made a choice for Jesus. Perhaps they are not yet saved, but they are sanctified.

23
00:54:04.418 --> 00:54:11.418
That means we can pray for them. We can pronounce blessings over them. We can speak the blood of Jesus over them.

24
00:54:11.418 --> 00:54:18.418
So that they can be blessed and protected. So that the Holy Spirit also has time to come to them.

25
00:54:18.418 --> 00:54:26.418
Maybe your children are teenagers and you think to yourself, yes this is really a time to pray for them. But parents of small children, pray for them even now.

26
00:54:27.418 --> 00:54:32.418
My children are only eight and ten, but I pray daily for them that they will accept Jesus.

27
00:54:32.418 --> 00:54:37.418
I do not like what they do, as long as they have Jesus. As long as they have Jesus.

28
00:54:49.418 --> 00:54:51.418
Glory to Jesus.

29
00:54:55.418 --> 00:54:57.418
Glory to Jesus.

30
00:55:03.418 --> 00:55:11.418
Lord, I want to pray to you lastly that the gospel, the good news of Jesus will be known in the area where we live.

31
00:55:12.418 --> 00:55:22.418
Lord, I want to pray that the people of Open Church that it does not stop here. I want to pray in the name of Jesus that the gospel will penetrate into the streets of the Kempen where we are.

32
00:55:23.418 --> 00:55:27.418
Lord, I want to pray that the good news is Jesus Christ is Savior and Lord.

33
00:55:28.418 --> 00:55:31.418
Lord, that this will reign in these streets of the Kempen.

34
00:55:32.418 --> 00:55:37.418
Lord, that it will go through the streets and that He will use us for that in the mighty name of Jesus.

35
00:55:38.418 --> 00:55:39.418
Can we say amen to that?

36
00:55:40.418 --> 00:55:41.418
Can we say amen to that?

37
00:55:42.418 --> 00:55:44.418
Amen, amen. Give Jesus a round of applause.

38
00:55:45.418 --> 00:55:46.418
Hallelujah.

39
00:55:50.418 --> 00:55:53.418
Perhaps this is a moment that we can say thoughts to each other.

40
00:55:54.418 --> 00:55:58.418
Give each other a hand. Greet each other for a moment in the name of Jesus.

41
00:56:02.418 --> 00:56:05.418
Glory to Jesus. Let's get to know each other for a moment.

42
00:56:24.418 --> 00:56:25.418
Glory to Jesus.

43
00:56:35.418 --> 00:56:40.418
Are there any guests in our church today? Are there people here in the church who are here for the first time today?

44
00:56:41.418 --> 00:56:42.418
Raise your hand.

45
00:56:43.418 --> 00:56:45.418
There I see someone, let's give applause for all our guests.

46
00:56:46.418 --> 00:56:50.418
Welcome to the church. Welcome to Open Church.

47
00:56:54.418 --> 00:56:55.418
Hallelujah.

48
00:56:57.418 --> 00:56:58.418
I have an announcement to read here.

49
00:57:00.418 --> 00:57:04.418
The Christmas service of Open Church is on December 22.

50
00:57:05.418 --> 00:57:08.418
The Christmas service of Open Church is on December 22.

51
00:57:09.418 --> 00:57:13.418
As a church, we find it important that family life is also present.

52
00:57:14.418 --> 00:57:21.418
And that's why we have chosen to have services on December 25, on the evening of December 24 or in the morning.

53
00:57:22.418 --> 00:57:25.418
You can hold five services on all those days.

54
00:57:26.418 --> 00:57:31.418
We choose as a church to say to the church.

55
00:57:32.418 --> 00:57:36.418
Make sure you are in church 52 Sundays a year.

56
00:57:37.418 --> 00:57:39.418
Unless you are on vacation or something.

57
00:57:40.418 --> 00:57:41.418
Or have to be away for work.

58
00:57:41.418 --> 00:57:42.418
Make sure you are in church.

59
00:57:43.418 --> 00:57:48.418
And we want to fill those days, those Sunday mornings, with the glory of Jesus.

60
00:57:49.418 --> 00:57:52.418
And we want to equip the people with everything they need.

61
00:57:53.418 --> 00:57:57.418
And that is why we have chosen to always hold the Christmas services.

62
00:57:58.418 --> 00:58:01.418
Those closest to Christmas, before Christmas, and then still do some afterwards.

63
00:58:02.418 --> 00:58:04.418
Then you are completely full of food and such. We do those.

64
00:58:05.418 --> 00:58:09.418
We always hold the Christmas service before Christmas, as close to Christmas as possible.

65
00:58:09.418 --> 00:58:10.418
So this year, December 22nd.

66
00:58:11.418 --> 00:58:16.418
Come there yourself. Bring someone along. But I always want to say, definitely bring people along.

67
00:58:17.418 --> 00:58:18.418
Wonderful. Hallelujah.

68
00:58:19.418 --> 00:58:20.418
Does everyone have a seat?

69
00:58:21.418 --> 00:58:25.418
I see that lately many people are standing in the overflow back there, in the bar.

70
00:58:26.418 --> 00:58:30.418
So I just really want to say to us always, when you come to church in the morning.

71
00:58:31.418 --> 00:58:34.418
Try to always cozy up together as much as possible.

72
00:58:35.418 --> 00:58:37.418
We are working on a new building.

73
00:58:37.418 --> 00:58:39.418
Only that is still 3 million euros further.

74
00:58:40.418 --> 00:58:41.418
Nice.

75
00:58:42.418 --> 00:58:44.418
If someone has that, call me.

76
00:58:45.418 --> 00:58:46.418
It will be fine.

77
00:58:47.418 --> 00:58:48.418
Ruben can invite you.

78
00:58:54.418 --> 00:58:55.418
Good morning.

79
00:58:57.418 --> 00:58:59.418
I indeed get to say something about giving.

80
00:59:01.418 --> 00:59:04.418
And actually giving, what is that really?

81
00:59:04.418 --> 00:59:07.418
That is actually showing God that you have a grateful heart.

82
00:59:09.418 --> 00:59:15.418
That is showing Him that He also comes first in that area, in that financial area.

83
00:59:17.418 --> 00:59:20.418
And actually, when you look at giving from that perspective.

84
00:59:22.418 --> 00:59:28.418
That is why you can also put God first in that.

85
00:59:28.418 --> 00:59:30.418
Then you will receive blessings from that.

86
00:59:33.418 --> 00:59:36.418
And actually, that is what God always challenges us to do.

87
00:59:37.418 --> 00:59:39.418
Because that may sound strange when I say that.

88
00:59:39.418 --> 00:59:40.418
Does God challenge us?

89
00:59:40.418 --> 00:59:42.418
Yes, He absolutely challenges us.

90
00:59:43.418 --> 00:59:45.418
To make the right choices.

91
00:59:47.418 --> 00:59:48.418
I don't know if you know it.

92
00:59:48.418 --> 00:59:51.418
In the Bible, it says something like, yes, your blessing is a blessing.

93
00:59:52.418 --> 00:59:53.418
But that is not the case.

94
00:59:54.418 --> 00:59:55.418
I don't know if you know it.

95
00:59:55.418 --> 01:00:00.418
In the Bible, it says something like, your body is a temple of the Holy Spirit.

96
01:00:01.418 --> 01:00:06.418
Make sure that your body and every part of your body is a weapon of righteousness.

97
01:00:08.418 --> 01:00:10.418
And it is exactly the same with giving.

98
01:00:10.418 --> 01:00:12.418
That is showing that we are grateful.

99
01:00:13.418 --> 01:00:17.418
That we give back a part of what God has already given us.

100
01:00:18.418 --> 01:00:23.418
And I want to go with you to Matthew 6:20 to 21.

101
01:00:26.418 --> 01:00:28.418
For giving is a blessing.

102
01:00:30.418 --> 01:00:32.418
Giving is a privilege.

103
01:00:34.418 --> 01:00:37.418
And it also shows where our true priority lies.

104
01:00:38.418 --> 01:00:43.418
And when we look at Matthew 6 verses 20 and 21.

105
01:00:43.418 --> 01:00:45.418
Store up for yourselves treasures in heaven.

106
01:00:47.418 --> 01:00:50.418
Those treasures do not perish through moths and rust.

107
01:00:51.418 --> 01:00:54.418
And there are no thieves who break in or steal.

108
01:00:55.418 --> 01:00:56.418
Remember well.

109
01:00:57.418 --> 01:01:01.418
Where your treasures are, there your heart will be also.

110
01:01:01.418 --> 01:01:04.418
And this is about gathering heavenly treasures.

111
01:01:04.418 --> 01:01:05.418
And we know that well.

112
01:01:05.418 --> 01:01:06.418
Most of us know that.

113
01:01:06.418 --> 01:01:08.418
Perhaps some do not.

114
01:01:09.418 --> 01:01:11.418
Then I will explain it a little bit.

115
01:01:12.418 --> 01:01:21.418
If you ask yourself, how can you convert your natural goods into something spiritual?

116
01:01:23.418 --> 01:01:26.418
You do this by giving your money, for example.

117
01:01:27.418 --> 01:01:35.418
For with that money, with your contribution, the gospel can be proclaimed here in this area.

118
01:01:36.418 --> 01:01:38.418
Can we reach people?

119
01:01:38.418 --> 01:01:42.418
And as I look at you and see the room now, and it is so full.

120
01:01:43.418 --> 01:01:48.418
I truly feel that responsibility we have as leaders over you.

121
01:01:48.418 --> 01:01:51.418
We want to teach you things, we want to bring you closer to God.

122
01:01:51.418 --> 01:01:54.418
And this piece is also part of that.

123
01:01:55.418 --> 01:01:58.418
Let your God be seen in everything that He is first.

124
01:01:59.418 --> 01:02:05.418
And then you are able to contribute to the salvation of people.

125
01:02:06.418 --> 01:02:09.418
And those are exactly treasures in heaven.

126
01:02:10.418 --> 01:02:12.418
You are a treasure in heaven.

127
01:02:13.418 --> 01:02:17.418
Someone once told you how much Jesus loves you.

128
01:02:19.418 --> 01:02:22.418
Someone once told you, make a choice.

129
01:02:23.418 --> 01:02:25.418
Choose what is good.

130
01:02:27.418 --> 01:02:29.418
Choose what is good.

131
01:02:29.418 --> 01:02:31.418
He loves you all.

132
01:02:31.418 --> 01:02:34.418
I want to pray for the collection, for giving.

133
01:02:34.418 --> 01:02:36.418
For it is truly a matter of the heart.

134
01:02:36.418 --> 01:02:42.418
It has nothing to do with the fact that we as a church are eager to receive this money.

135
01:02:42.418 --> 01:02:49.418
It has to do with a matter of the heart and our vision to proclaim Jesus in this area.

136
01:02:50.418 --> 01:02:52.418
Lord God, I want to honor You.

137
01:02:53.418 --> 01:02:56.418
I want to thank You for who You are.

138
01:02:57.418 --> 01:03:03.418
I want to pray, Lord God, that we always put You in that first place.

139
01:03:04.418 --> 01:03:06.418
In every area of our lives.

140
01:03:08.418 --> 01:03:13.418
If we do that, then You promise blessing.

141
01:03:14.418 --> 01:03:17.418
Then we will truly see who our provider is.

142
01:03:18.418 --> 01:03:23.418
Then we will truly discover how great your love for us is.

143
01:03:23.418 --> 01:03:30.418
I want to pray, Lord God, that we, as Western people living here, are so attached to our money.

144
01:03:31.418 --> 01:03:33.418
Lord God, that we bring this to you as well.

145
01:03:34.418 --> 01:03:36.418
And truly put our trust in you.

146
01:03:38.418 --> 01:03:40.418
You are the one who gives.

147
01:03:41.418 --> 01:03:43.418
Lord God, and we give back.

148
01:03:43.418 --> 01:03:45.418
And we want to give back.

149
01:03:45.418 --> 01:03:47.418
It is what our heart desires.

150
01:03:47.418 --> 01:03:49.418
And what you work out in our hearts.

151
01:03:49.418 --> 01:03:51.418
And what you work out in our hearts.

152
01:03:51.418 --> 01:03:54.418
And I want to bless every contribution.

153
01:03:55.418 --> 01:04:01.418
Lord God, and our promise, Lord God, as a church, is to handle it carefully.

154
01:04:02.418 --> 01:04:08.418
And to ensure that your kingdom finds expansion here in Lommel.

155
01:04:08.418 --> 01:04:11.418
In Jesus' name. Amen. Amen.

156
01:04:20.418 --> 01:04:22.418
Christ will bring the Word.

157
01:04:23.418 --> 01:04:24.418
Hallelujah.

158
01:04:27.418 --> 01:04:30.418
Before we begin with the Word, I want to give a short testimony.

159
01:04:30.418 --> 01:04:34.418
Last Friday, I was with my family, with friends in Antwerp.

160
01:04:34.418 --> 01:04:36.418
To fill a pleasant evening.

161
01:04:36.418 --> 01:04:42.418
On our way back, the navigation directed us through Geel and then Mol.

162
01:04:42.418 --> 01:04:48.418
At a certain point there at the intersection of Mol, where that McDonald's is, you all know it.

163
01:04:48.418 --> 01:04:51.418
I was driving the full 95 km per hour.

164
01:04:51.418 --> 01:04:53.418
To avoid getting flashed, you know how it is.

165
01:04:53.418 --> 01:04:57.418
I was just driving the full 90 km per hour on the ring road.

166
01:04:57.418 --> 01:04:59.418
It was green.

167
01:04:59.418 --> 01:05:01.418
So for us, there was nothing wrong.

168
01:05:01.418 --> 01:05:05.418
But the moment I crossed that intersection, someone came full speed.

169
01:05:05.418 --> 01:05:07.418
Really, literally full speed.

170
01:05:07.418 --> 01:05:10.418
I have never pressed the brakes of my car so hard.

171
01:05:10.418 --> 01:05:12.418
I have a safe car.

172
01:05:12.418 --> 01:05:16.418
Only at 90 km per hour, you realize at that moment how long the stopping distance is.

173
01:05:16.418 --> 01:05:18.418
We would have collided head-on.

174
01:05:18.418 --> 01:05:20.418
That would have been an ugly crash.

175
01:05:20.418 --> 01:05:22.418
Really, it would have been ugly.

176
01:05:22.418 --> 01:05:24.418
But it really came.

177
01:05:24.418 --> 01:05:26.418
I had pressed it so hard.

178
01:05:26.418 --> 01:05:28.418
I had pressed it so hard.

179
01:05:28.418 --> 01:05:30.418
I had pressed it so hard.

180
01:05:30.418 --> 01:05:32.418
I had pressed it so hard.

181
01:05:32.418 --> 01:05:34.418
I really pressed it so hard.

182
01:05:34.418 --> 01:05:36.418
It would have been ugly.

183
01:05:36.418 --> 01:05:38.418
But it really came.

184
01:05:38.418 --> 01:05:40.418
That's how we ended up together. Literally.

185
01:05:40.418 --> 01:05:42.418
And that ambulance guy looks at us.

186
01:05:42.418 --> 01:05:44.418
And he does like this.

187
01:05:44.418 --> 01:05:46.418
And I like this.

188
01:05:48.418 --> 01:05:50.418
But it was.

189
01:05:50.418 --> 01:05:52.418
I have looked up crazy things in my life.

190
01:05:52.418 --> 01:05:54.418
But that was a crazy moment.

191
01:05:54.418 --> 01:05:57.418
But the moment you then recover from the shock.

192
01:05:57.418 --> 01:05:59.418
And drive back home.

193
01:05:59.418 --> 01:06:01.418
Then you give glory to Jesus.

194
01:06:02.418 --> 01:06:04.418
You can reason with yourself then.

195
01:06:04.418 --> 01:06:06.418
Oh yes, that was the car. Oh yes, that was coincidence.

196
01:06:06.418 --> 01:06:08.418
Oh yes, that worked out well.

197
01:06:08.418 --> 01:06:10.418
You can say all those things.

198
01:06:10.418 --> 01:06:12.418
I choose to say.

199
01:06:12.418 --> 01:06:14.418
Thank you, Jesus.

200
01:06:14.418 --> 01:06:16.418
Thank you for setting us free.

201
01:06:16.418 --> 01:06:18.418
Thank you for protecting us.

202
01:06:19.418 --> 01:06:22.418
I believe in the presence of angels.

203
01:06:22.418 --> 01:06:25.418
I believe in the presence of angels who care for me.

204
01:06:25.418 --> 01:06:29.418
I believe in the protection of the blood of Jesus over my life.

205
01:06:29.418 --> 01:06:32.418
That does not mean you should seek out danger in life.

206
01:06:32.418 --> 01:06:34.418
Never test God in your life.

207
01:06:34.418 --> 01:06:37.418
But know that there is a God who loves you.

208
01:06:37.418 --> 01:06:39.418
Who cares for you and protects you.

209
01:06:39.418 --> 01:06:41.418
And be engaged with that daily.

210
01:06:41.418 --> 01:06:44.418
Thank God for the great things in your life.

211
01:06:44.418 --> 01:06:48.418
Thank Him that He has freed you from sin and unrighteousness.

212
01:06:48.418 --> 01:06:52.418
But also thank Him for all the blessings in life.

213
01:06:52.418 --> 01:06:54.418
Thank Him for your job.

214
01:06:54.418 --> 01:06:56.418
Thank Him for your family.

215
01:06:56.418 --> 01:06:58.418
Thank Him for your marriage.

216
01:06:58.418 --> 01:07:01.418
Thank Him for everything that is important and unimportant.

217
01:07:01.418 --> 01:07:03.418
Just thank, thank, thank.

218
01:07:03.418 --> 01:07:07.418
Let us please be a grateful congregation.

219
01:07:07.418 --> 01:07:10.418
That we always come to Him and say thank you, Lord.

220
01:07:10.418 --> 01:07:15.418
That you protected me at that crossroads from something that could have been a very ugly accident.

221
01:07:15.418 --> 01:07:17.418
God is a good God.

222
01:07:17.418 --> 01:07:19.418
And He is very closely involved with us humans.

223
01:07:19.418 --> 01:07:21.418
We do not have a distant God.

224
01:07:21.418 --> 01:07:25.418
A big spirit in the sky who is distant from His people.

225
01:07:25.418 --> 01:07:29.418
No, we have a God who is so involved in your life.

226
01:07:29.418 --> 01:07:35.418
That God sent the Holy Spirit because He wanted to be so close that He came to dwell in you.

227
01:07:35.418 --> 01:07:36.418
So close is God.

228
01:07:36.418 --> 01:07:40.418
Let us honor Him with all that we are and all that we have. Amen.

229
01:07:40.418 --> 01:07:42.418
Chris, may I invite you?

230
01:07:42.418 --> 01:07:46.418
Make some applause for our best Chris. Hallelujah.

231
01:07:47.418 --> 01:07:49.418
Thank you very much.

232
01:07:54.418 --> 01:07:56.418
Hallelujah.

233
01:07:57.418 --> 01:07:59.418
God is so good.

234
01:08:00.418 --> 01:08:03.418
I find it nice to start the Word with prayer.

235
01:08:03.418 --> 01:08:06.418
Maybe it's nice to stand up for a moment.

236
01:08:09.418 --> 01:08:11.418
Thank you, Lord, for Your Word.

237
01:08:12.418 --> 01:08:14.418
Lord, You are the Word Yourself.

238
01:08:15.418 --> 01:08:17.418
Lord, the Word is spirit and life.

239
01:08:17.418 --> 01:08:19.418
Lord, You are spirit and life.

240
01:08:19.418 --> 01:08:22.418
Lord, You distribute Your Word time and again.

241
01:08:22.418 --> 01:08:25.418
And when you share your Word each time, you share yourself.

242
01:08:25.418 --> 01:08:27.418
Lord, that is who you are.

243
01:08:27.418 --> 01:08:29.418
Lord, you would not be yourself.

244
01:08:29.418 --> 01:08:37.418
Lord, I thank you that through your own Holy Spirit, we may come to know you and your calling better and better.

245
01:08:37.418 --> 01:08:40.418
Lord, I pray this in the name of King Jesus.

246
01:08:40.418 --> 01:08:41.418
Amen.

247
01:08:42.418 --> 01:08:44.418
Hallelujah.

248
01:08:45.418 --> 01:08:49.418
We have been bought, saved, and paid for by the blood of Jesus.

249
01:08:49.418 --> 01:08:51.418
That is good news.

250
01:08:51.418 --> 01:08:55.418
And that applies to everyone who sincerely believes in Jesus.

251
01:08:55.418 --> 01:08:57.418
And Pastor Tim, who started with that text.

252
01:08:57.418 --> 01:09:02.418
I find that very nice, because I actually wanted to use this text as an example of what I wanted to say.

253
01:09:02.418 --> 01:09:04.418
So that works out very well.

254
01:09:04.418 --> 01:09:07.418
It could very well be in the same spirit.

255
01:09:07.418 --> 01:09:11.418
And when we look at that text, John 3 verse 16, it says.

256
01:09:11.418 --> 01:09:16.418
For God so loved the world that he gave his only Son.

257
01:09:16.418 --> 01:09:21.418
That whoever believes in him shall not perish but have eternal life.

258
01:09:21.418 --> 01:09:27.418
And every evangelist will say, on that word world, for God so loved the world.

259
01:09:27.418 --> 01:09:29.418
Can you fill in your name?

260
01:09:29.418 --> 01:09:31.418
And that is true.

261
01:09:31.418 --> 01:09:33.418
That is completely true.

262
01:09:33.418 --> 01:09:35.418
If Tommy says it's true, then it is true.

263
01:09:36.418 --> 01:09:39.418
And it is really true, because God's Word says so too.

264
01:09:39.418 --> 01:09:42.418
For we are also part of this world.

265
01:09:42.418 --> 01:09:49.418
But what I actually want to say is that God's plan is indeed greater than you and me.

266
01:09:49.418 --> 01:09:55.418
And it is very important to adopt His plan, His greater plan, in our hearts.

267
01:09:55.418 --> 01:10:02.418
For if we do that, and if we gain a better perspective on it, we will also understand Him better.

268
01:10:02.418 --> 01:10:09.418
And if we understand Him better, we will also understand what that calling is, that God has, that Jesus Himself has.

269
01:10:09.418 --> 01:10:11.418
And that He also wants to give to us.

270
01:10:11.418 --> 01:10:13.418
For we have a calling.

271
01:10:13.418 --> 01:10:19.418
It is very important, and it is truly a matter of life and death, that we are saved, bought and paid for.

272
01:10:19.418 --> 01:10:21.418
And that is His work.

273
01:10:21.418 --> 01:10:23.418
And that is why we are here too.

274
01:10:23.418 --> 01:10:27.418
But we also have a part to play in that calling.

275
01:10:27.418 --> 01:10:31.418
We may go further than just being saved and barely making it over the line.

276
01:10:31.418 --> 01:10:34.418
And we have already heard a lot about this this morning.

277
01:10:34.418 --> 01:10:42.418
But if our perspective of God's plan becomes greater, then we will also sow more carefully.

278
01:10:42.418 --> 01:10:44.418
Then we will also manage our time more carefully.

279
01:10:44.418 --> 01:10:46.418
Then we will also think more carefully.

280
01:10:46.418 --> 01:10:52.418
And then the harvest of everyone's life and of the whole church will also be better.

281
01:10:52.418 --> 01:10:54.418
Is then also greater.

282
01:10:54.418 --> 01:10:56.418
Is then also the intention.

283
01:10:56.418 --> 01:10:57.418
And that is what it is about.

284
01:10:57.418 --> 01:11:00.418
For what sin is, is that you miss the intention.

285
01:11:00.418 --> 01:11:02.418
But we actually want to achieve the intention.

286
01:11:02.418 --> 01:11:05.418
In the past month, we have talked about it.

287
01:11:05.418 --> 01:11:11.418
If we run after ourselves and do our own things, then we miss that intention.

288
01:11:11.418 --> 01:11:16.418
And now the intention of today is to discover His intention.

289
01:11:16.418 --> 01:11:17.418
To discover more.

290
01:11:17.418 --> 01:11:23.418
So that we can go further than just being saved, which is already a miracle in itself, of course.

291
01:11:24.418 --> 01:11:31.418
And the beauty of it is that the calling of Christ is restoration, is healing.

292
01:11:31.418 --> 01:11:34.418
And not only for us, but also for others.

293
01:11:34.418 --> 01:11:37.418
And that is very beautiful to be able to see.

294
01:11:37.418 --> 01:11:42.418
And that is why I want to call this sermon, Jesus Christ alone.

295
01:11:42.418 --> 01:11:44.418
Or through Jesus Christ alone.

296
01:11:44.418 --> 01:11:46.418
And this morning it was said so often.

297
01:11:46.418 --> 01:11:48.418
It is indeed through Jesus alone.

298
01:11:48.418 --> 01:11:51.418
And what follows is the true cornerstone.

299
01:11:51.418 --> 01:11:56.418
That is the theme of Jesus, the piece of Jesus that we may address today.

300
01:11:56.418 --> 01:12:02.418
And I think it is very good to take a moment to reflect on that text that we have dealt with over the past year.

301
01:12:02.418 --> 01:12:08.418
Certainly now that we are also heading towards Christmas, we have a period of perhaps reflection.

302
01:12:08.418 --> 01:12:11.418
Is it good to let this text sink in once again?

303
01:12:11.418 --> 01:12:13.418
I do not know if it is already present.

304
01:12:13.418 --> 01:12:17.418
1 Peter 2, verses 1 to 8.

305
01:12:21.418 --> 01:12:26.418
And actually, this text has been a piece of Bible study by Peter.

306
01:12:26.418 --> 01:12:31.418
And Peter did not have Google or a Bible app.

307
01:12:31.418 --> 01:12:35.418
Where you can easily find texts together under a certain theme.

308
01:12:35.418 --> 01:12:39.418
But he really had to search through those scrolls.

309
01:12:39.418 --> 01:12:41.418
And they had to be rolled and used.

310
01:12:41.418 --> 01:12:47.418
And you can see that actually this text has been a piece of Bible study by Peter.

311
01:12:47.418 --> 01:12:51.418
For he connects different texts together about that cornerstone.

312
01:12:51.418 --> 01:12:54.418
So nice to see.

313
01:12:54.418 --> 01:12:56.418
I will just read it out loud.

314
01:12:56.418 --> 01:12:59.418
So rid yourselves of all that is bad.

315
01:12:59.418 --> 01:13:02.418
Of all deceit and hypocrisy.

316
01:13:02.418 --> 01:13:05.418
All envy and slander.

317
01:13:05.418 --> 01:13:09.418
And crave like newborn infants the pure milk of the Word.

318
01:13:09.418 --> 01:13:11.418
Food.

319
01:13:11.418 --> 01:13:14.418
So that you may grow thereby and attain your salvation.

320
01:13:14.418 --> 01:13:17.418
You have tasted the goodness of the Lord.

321
01:13:17.418 --> 01:13:19.418
Join him.

322
01:13:19.418 --> 01:13:21.418
By the living stone.

323
01:13:21.418 --> 01:13:23.418
Rejected by men.

324
01:13:23.418 --> 01:13:26.418
But chosen by God for his preciousness.

325
01:13:26.418 --> 01:13:30.418
And let yourselves also be used as living stones.

326
01:13:30.418 --> 01:13:33.418
For the building of a spiritual temple.

327
01:13:33.418 --> 01:13:36.418
Form a holy priesthood.

328
01:13:36.418 --> 01:13:38.418
To offer spiritual sacrifices.

329
01:13:38.418 --> 01:13:41.418
That are pleasing to God through Jesus.

330
01:13:42.418 --> 01:13:45.418
And then he says, for it is written in Scripture.

331
01:13:45.418 --> 01:13:47.418
That was what he looked up.

332
01:13:47.418 --> 01:13:51.418
If you are taking notes, that comes from Isaiah 28 verse 16.

333
01:13:51.418 --> 01:13:52.418
Then he says.

334
01:13:52.418 --> 01:13:54.418
In Zion I lay a cornerstone.

335
01:13:54.418 --> 01:13:57.418
That I have chosen for its preciousness.

336
01:13:57.418 --> 01:14:00.418
Whoever trusts in it will not be put to shame.

337
01:14:00.418 --> 01:14:02.418
Another translation says.

338
01:14:02.418 --> 01:14:05.418
Needs to seek no other refuge.

339
01:14:05.418 --> 01:14:07.418
Precious is he to you.

340
01:14:07.418 --> 01:14:09.418
Whoever trusts in it.

341
01:14:09.418 --> 01:14:11.418
So if you trust in him.

342
01:14:11.418 --> 01:14:14.418
However, those who do not trust in him.

343
01:14:14.418 --> 01:14:16.418
The stone that the builders rejected.

344
01:14:16.418 --> 01:14:18.418
Has become the cornerstone.

345
01:14:18.418 --> 01:14:22.418
And that comes from Psalm 118 verse 22.

346
01:14:22.418 --> 01:14:26.418
And then Peter continues with Isaiah 8 verse 14.

347
01:14:26.418 --> 01:14:27.418
And then he says.

348
01:14:27.418 --> 01:14:30.418
And about the two kingdoms of Israel.

349
01:14:30.418 --> 01:14:31.418
He says.

350
01:14:31.418 --> 01:14:34.418
It is a stone over which one stumbles.

351
01:14:34.418 --> 01:14:36.418
A rock that one strikes against.

352
01:14:36.418 --> 01:14:40.418
They stumble because they refuse to obey God's Word.

353
01:14:40.418 --> 01:14:42.418
To this they are destined.

354
01:14:42.418 --> 01:14:44.418
This is a strong text.

355
01:14:44.418 --> 01:14:46.418
But an important text.

356
01:14:46.418 --> 01:14:49.418
If you have read John 3 verse 16 and 17.

357
01:14:49.418 --> 01:14:50.418
But you read further.

358
01:14:50.418 --> 01:14:51.418
Then it says.

359
01:14:51.418 --> 01:14:53.418
The one who does not choose Jesus.

360
01:14:53.418 --> 01:14:55.418
Is judging himself.

361
01:14:55.418 --> 01:14:57.418
And that is actually what is written here.

362
01:14:57.418 --> 01:14:59.418
And then it says afterwards.

363
01:14:59.418 --> 01:15:01.418
But you.

364
01:15:01.418 --> 01:15:03.418
That is us.

365
01:15:03.418 --> 01:15:05.418
Are a chosen generation.

366
01:15:05.418 --> 01:15:07.418
A kingdom of priests.

367
01:15:07.418 --> 01:15:09.418
A holy nation.

368
01:15:09.418 --> 01:15:11.418
A people that God has acquired for Himself.

369
01:15:11.418 --> 01:15:14.418
To proclaim the great deeds of Him.

370
01:15:14.418 --> 01:15:16.418
Who called you out of darkness.

371
01:15:16.418 --> 01:15:20.418
Into His marvelous light.

372
01:15:20.418 --> 01:15:22.418
Once you were not a people.

373
01:15:22.418 --> 01:15:25.418
Once we did not count at all.

374
01:15:25.418 --> 01:15:26.418
We were useless.

375
01:15:26.418 --> 01:15:28.418
We were discarded.

376
01:15:28.418 --> 01:15:30.418
But now we are God's people.

377
01:15:30.418 --> 01:15:32.418
And what does He say then?

378
01:15:32.418 --> 01:15:34.418
Once you were denied compassion.

379
01:15:34.418 --> 01:15:38.418
So compassion is actually protection and cherishing.

380
01:15:38.418 --> 01:15:42.418
And now we receive God's compassion and cherishing.

381
01:15:42.418 --> 01:15:44.418
God's compassion.

382
01:15:44.418 --> 01:15:46.418
How beautiful is this?

383
01:15:46.418 --> 01:15:48.418
It is safe with God.

384
01:15:48.418 --> 01:15:53.418
And that Bible study of Peter.

385
01:15:53.418 --> 01:15:55.418
Also a blessing of full-time ministry.

386
01:15:55.418 --> 01:15:56.418
Very important.

387
01:15:56.418 --> 01:15:59.418
Is even now a blessing for us.

388
01:15:59.418 --> 01:16:01.418
This text is a blessing for us.

389
01:16:01.418 --> 01:16:05.418
He explains how it works with God.

390
01:16:05.418 --> 01:16:07.418
And as I just look through the Bible.

391
01:16:07.418 --> 01:16:09.418
And I do look through my Bible app.

392
01:16:09.418 --> 01:16:12.418
Then I see about 12.5 texts about that cornerstone.

393
01:16:12.418 --> 01:16:14.418
Yes, that's nice.

394
01:16:14.418 --> 01:16:17.418
But if we look very closely and read well.

395
01:16:17.418 --> 01:16:23.418
Then we see the principle of that cornerstone coming back in many places.

396
01:16:23.418 --> 01:16:25.418
And why is that?

397
01:16:25.418 --> 01:16:28.418
That is because Jesus himself is the Word.

398
01:16:28.418 --> 01:16:29.418
He is the cornerstone himself.

399
01:16:29.418 --> 01:16:31.418
He is also the temple.

400
01:16:31.418 --> 01:16:32.418
He is actually everything.

401
01:16:32.418 --> 01:16:38.418
So it's not strange that you can find things to talk about Jesus.

402
01:16:38.418 --> 01:16:39.418
About the true cornerstone.

403
01:16:39.418 --> 01:16:45.418
And that's why I want to take a piece this morning.

404
01:16:45.418 --> 01:16:49.418
Because otherwise, I think we would only be ready when Jesus returns.

405
01:16:49.418 --> 01:16:52.418
And I wanted to spare you that for this time.

406
01:16:52.418 --> 01:16:54.418
Because there is also onion soup that has been prepared.

407
01:16:54.418 --> 01:17:03.418
And this morning it is so beautiful to see that calling, that also lies in that cornerstone.

408
01:17:03.418 --> 01:17:05.418
We will see that.

409
01:17:05.418 --> 01:17:08.418
And last week Pastor Tim already mentioned it.

410
01:17:08.418 --> 01:17:10.418
At the end of his sermon as well.

411
01:17:10.418 --> 01:17:14.418
That you have two different worlds.

412
01:17:14.418 --> 01:17:16.418
Of good and of evil.

413
01:17:16.418 --> 01:17:17.418
And that started with Adam.

414
01:17:17.418 --> 01:17:19.418
That started with the children of Adam.

415
01:17:19.418 --> 01:17:21.418
One killed the other.

416
01:17:21.418 --> 01:17:25.418
With Noah, you also see good and evil happening all the time.

417
01:17:25.418 --> 01:17:28.418
Then he also mentioned Abram.

418
01:17:28.418 --> 01:17:32.418
Who God took out of the land of idolatry.

419
01:17:32.418 --> 01:17:36.418
Also a very beautiful image of what He has done for us.

420
01:17:36.418 --> 01:17:39.418
Just to start anew.

421
01:17:39.418 --> 01:17:42.418
And that is what he wants now as well.

422
01:17:42.418 --> 01:17:47.418
And now, not to stay with Abram, I want to continue with his grandson.

423
01:17:47.418 --> 01:17:49.418
That is Jacob.

424
01:17:49.418 --> 01:17:54.418
And that is such a wonderfully beautiful story.

425
01:17:54.418 --> 01:17:59.418
In which God once again shares His plan and calling with Jacob.

426
01:17:59.418 --> 01:18:02.418
It is truly an intimate moment.

427
01:18:02.418 --> 01:18:06.418
And I want to read it together in Genesis 28.

428
01:18:06.418 --> 01:18:10.418
Verses 10 to 22.

429
01:18:12.418 --> 01:18:17.418
You see such a beautiful image of the cornerstone.

430
01:18:18.418 --> 01:18:21.418
The true cornerstone. Jesus.

431
01:18:25.418 --> 01:18:29.418
Jacob had caused a bit of trouble at home.

432
01:18:29.418 --> 01:18:32.418
He had taken his first birthright from Esau.

433
01:18:32.418 --> 01:18:38.418
And he had snatched the blessing in a less than honorable way from his brother.

434
01:18:38.418 --> 01:18:41.418
But he went for that blessing.

435
01:18:41.418 --> 01:18:46.418
He wanted to go. He wanted to pursue what God had for him.

436
01:18:46.418 --> 01:18:49.418
And Esau was like, just give me a bowl of soup.

437
01:18:49.418 --> 01:18:53.418
And then you also see those two differences.

438
01:18:53.418 --> 01:19:00.418
Later in the Bible, you also see that God says He loved Jacob and hated Esau.

439
01:19:00.418 --> 01:19:04.418
And he fled, for Esau was in a state of rage.

440
01:19:04.418 --> 01:19:07.418
He really wanted to do something terrible to him.

441
01:19:07.418 --> 01:19:10.418
So he thought, we are on our way.

442
01:19:10.418 --> 01:19:14.418
And he had understood from his mother where he needed to go to find a wife.

443
01:19:14.418 --> 01:19:17.418
He ended up with two, but that's alright.

444
01:19:17.418 --> 01:19:24.418
When I look, Jacob left Beersheba and went on his way to Haran.

445
01:19:24.418 --> 01:19:31.418
And on his journey, he came to a place where he stayed overnight, because the sun had already set.

446
01:19:31.418 --> 01:19:36.418
And he took one of those stones and laid it down.

447
01:19:36.418 --> 01:19:38.418
And he laid it under his head.

448
01:19:38.418 --> 01:19:40.418
And he went to lie down in that place.

449
01:19:40.418 --> 01:19:43.418
And then I see such an image of a stone.

450
01:19:43.418 --> 01:19:45.418
Yes, I would prefer a pillow.

451
01:19:45.418 --> 01:19:50.418
But he took a stone and then I actually see him embracing that stone.

452
01:19:50.418 --> 01:19:52.418
And then I actually see him lying on it.

453
01:19:52.418 --> 01:19:57.418
And he rests his head on that stone.

454
01:19:57.418 --> 01:20:01.418
That is the image I get when I see and read this.

455
01:20:01.418 --> 01:20:03.418
And then he had a dream.

456
01:20:03.418 --> 01:20:08.418
And he saw a ladder that was set on the earth and reached all the way to heaven.

457
01:20:08.418 --> 01:20:13.418
And there he saw God's angels going up and down.

458
01:20:13.418 --> 01:20:17.418
And he also saw the Lord standing beside him.

459
01:20:17.418 --> 01:20:23.418
And He said, I am the Lord, the God of your ancestor Abram.

460
01:20:23.418 --> 01:20:27.418
I am the God of your grandfather, the God of Isaac, the God of your father.

461
01:20:27.418 --> 01:20:32.418
And the land on which you are now lying will I give to you and your descendants.

462
01:20:32.418 --> 01:20:37.418
And you will have as many descendants as there is dust on the earth.

463
01:20:37.418 --> 01:20:42.418
Your territory will extend to the west and to the east and to the north and to the south.

464
01:20:42.418 --> 01:20:49.418
And in you and in your descendants all the nations of the earth will be blessed.

465
01:20:49.418 --> 01:20:54.418
I am with you. I will protect you everywhere.

466
01:20:54.418 --> 01:20:56.418
Wherever you go.

467
01:20:56.418 --> 01:21:00.418
And I will bring you back to this land.

468
01:21:00.418 --> 01:21:05.418
I will not leave you until I have done what I have promised.

469
01:21:06.418 --> 01:21:07.418
So beautiful.

470
01:21:07.418 --> 01:21:09.418
And then Jacob woke up.

471
01:21:09.418 --> 01:21:13.418
Surely, the Lord is in this place.

472
01:21:13.418 --> 01:21:15.418
I didn't realize that.

473
01:21:15.418 --> 01:21:19.418
He really didn't realize it. So he didn't know what was happening to him.

474
01:21:19.418 --> 01:21:22.418
And reverence filled him.

475
01:21:22.418 --> 01:21:24.418
He was truly filled with reverence.

476
01:21:24.418 --> 01:21:28.418
And he says, what an awe-inspiring place this is, he said.

477
01:21:28.418 --> 01:21:32.418
This is nothing but the house of God.

478
01:21:33.418 --> 01:21:36.418
This must be the gate of heaven.

479
01:21:36.418 --> 01:21:38.418
This is so prophetic.

480
01:21:38.418 --> 01:21:45.418
The next morning early, Jacob set up the stone he had used as a pillow.

481
01:21:45.418 --> 01:21:47.418
And he set him upright.

482
01:21:47.418 --> 01:21:51.418
And he anointed him by pouring oil over him.

483
01:21:51.418 --> 01:21:56.418
It is actually just priesthood in the making.

484
01:21:56.418 --> 01:21:59.418
And he named that place Bethel.

485
01:21:59.418 --> 01:22:01.418
But previously that city was called Les.

486
01:22:01.418 --> 01:22:09.418
There are even studies suggesting that Jacob did not choose the main road between the cities of Beersheba and Garan.

487
01:22:09.418 --> 01:22:13.418
But that he took a shortcut through Jebus.

488
01:22:13.418 --> 01:22:17.418
And that it would indeed have been on the spot of Mount Moriah.

489
01:22:17.418 --> 01:22:19.418
I find it all very beautiful.

490
01:22:19.418 --> 01:22:23.418
I would believe immediately, for it is a holy place.

491
01:22:23.418 --> 01:22:29.418
And that would ultimately become the place where David was allowed to build the temple.

492
01:22:29.418 --> 01:22:33.418
Not by someone from Israel, but chosen by God.

493
01:22:33.418 --> 01:22:35.418
Exactly at that spot where there was no Israel.

